<DocsPageTitle Path="Components/Skeleton" AddedVersion="1.7" AddedDate="2024-10-08">
    Blazorise Skeleton component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Show a preview of the page layout while its content is loading.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use skeleton placeholders when content takes time to load and users benefit from seeing where it will appear.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Structure
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A <Code>Skeleton</Code> groups <Code>SkeletonItem</Code> placeholders that define the shapes and sizes of the loading content.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsAnatomy Label="Skeleton component anatomy">
    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="Skeleton" Description="Contains the placeholder layout.">
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="SkeletonItem" Description="Defines one placeholder's shape and size." />
    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
</DocsAnatomy>

